## tracking/backlog

`plugins/tracking/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` is adapted from the `backlog` skill
in the `workflow` plugin of [umputun/cc-thingz](https://github.com/umputun/cc-thingz).

Retained as published: the fixed `docs/backlog/` store with one slug-named file
per item and no index, the `worth: yes | later | no` / `where` / `added`
frontmatter and the meaning of each value, the create-then-`git rm` lifecycle,
the slug argument, the read-verify-report-offer loop with `AskUserQuestion`, the
default-branch detection and the refusal to write onto another branch unasked,
dedupe on `where` then slug, the staged-index check before offering to commit,
and the rules section.

Changes made: `where` takes `path` or `path:symbol` instead of `path:line`, and
verification checks the symbol rather than the line; an admission gate was added
ahead of writing, with routing for findings that fail it (fix now, the status
board, a dated review's own register); the free body gained a contract — the
concrete run with real values, the misreading to prevent, options with costs
and a recommendation for a `later`, and a provenance line; the slug form is
`/tracking:backlog <slug>`; and the skill's triggers absorb those of the
`log-issue` skill it replaces.

